City of Surrey, Biodiversity Conservation Strategy, Appendix J
--------------------------------------------------------------

These columns of docs/deliverable/corridor_stress_ranking.csv are the City of
Surrey's text and attributes, not the author's:

    recommendation, ecological_value, risk_of_development, corridor_type,
    target_width_m

They are reproduced verbatim from Appendix J of the City of Surrey's
Biodiversity Conservation Strategy, pages 119-129 of the parent report:

    https://www.surrey.ca/sites/default/files/media/documents/Appendix_J.pdf

parsed by scripts/parse_appendix_j.py. The same attributes are also published by
the City on its open-data GIS layer. Copyright in all of it rests with the City
of Surrey. They are reproduced here under attribution because the corridor
ranking is not usable by a planner without them.

Everything else in that file is the author's and carries the repository's
licence: the CDEI values, the ranks, the percentiles and the priority flag.

Why this is a separate file
---------------------------

LICENSE is left as unmodified MIT text so that automated licence detection
(GitHub, Zenodo, licensee) continues to identify it correctly. Adding the
carve-out there would risk the repository being reported as "Other".
